# rASN-local ignore rules.
#
# rASN is developed as an independent project inside this repository and does not
# modify rDSN's own files, so rASN-specific ignore rules live here instead of the
# repository-root .gitignore.
#
# SCOPE LIMITATION (read before adding rules here). A nested .gitignore only
# applies below its own directory, so nothing in this file can ignore anything at
# the repository root. rASN's default durable-state, spilled-artifact, and JSONL
# trace paths are all *relative to the process working directory*, so a binary
# launched from the repository root would create an unignored `rasn/state`,
# `rasn/artifacts`, and `rasn/traces` there. Two consequences:
#
#   * Launch CodePilot / SREPilot / the runtime host from their binplaced
#     directory (builder/bin/<app>/) or from an install tree. rDSN's root
#     .gitignore already ignores `builder/` and `install/` wholesale.
#   * The shipped harnesses are self-contained and enforce this themselves:
#     tests/fault_injection/run_fault_injection.sh runs every child process in
#     its own output directory, and tests/integration/ allocates isolated
#     config/data/log trees per scenario.
#
# Likewise, a custom root-level build tree (e.g. `DSN_BUILD_DIR=builder-rasn
# ./run.sh build`, or `run.cmd build <type> <dir>` on Windows) cannot be ignored
# from here. Either point DSN_BUILD_DIR at a subdirectory of the already ignored
# `builder/`, or add the directory to your local .git/info/exclude.

# Durable state, spilled artifacts, and JSONL traces (see docs/DESIGN.md).
**/rasn/state/
**/rasn/artifacts/
**/rasn/traces/

# Replicated-state development profile data directory (config.rasn.state.ini).
**/rasn/state-cluster/

# Default output tree of the opt-in fault-injection harness (RASN_FI_OUT).
tests/fault_injection/out/

# LaTeX build products of the report (docs/report/build.sh).
docs/report/*.aux
docs/report/*.bbl
docs/report/*.blg
docs/report/*.fdb_latexmk
docs/report/*.fls
docs/report/*.log
docs/report/*.out
docs/report/*.pdf
docs/report/*.synctex.gz
